{
  "title": "Stage 4: Summaries",
  "summary": "Answer the questions a report is for with LINQ: totals, averages, per category and per month, in aligned columns.",
  "minutes": 25,
  "prereqs": [
    "csharp/06-generics-and-linq/04-linq-aggregates-and-grouping",
    "csharp/01-first-steps/04-strings"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "From a list to a report",
      "body": [
        "The program can now be trusted with any input. But printing every expense back is not a report. Nobody reads 400 lines to find out what the month cost.",
        "",
        "A report **answers questions**: how much in total, on what, and when? In this stage you answer them with LINQ and lay the numbers out in columns. This input has six good rows and five bad ones:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "date,category,amount,description",
        "2026-03-04,Travel,45.50,Taxi to airport",
        "2026-03-05,Meals,12.00,Lunch",
        "2026-03-05,Meals",
        "",
        "2026-03-06,Supplies,abc,Printer paper",
        "2026-03-07,Travel,120.00,Train to Leeds",
        "2026-03-09,Lodging,600.00,Hotel, 3 nights",
        "2026-13-01,Meals,20.00,Dinner",
        "2026-03-10,Parking,8.00,Car park",
        "2026-03-10,Meals,-5.00,Refund",
        "2026-03-11,Meals,65.20,Team dinner",
        "2026-04-02,meals,18.00,",
        "```",
        "",
        "and by the end of the stage it produces:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Expenses: 6",
        "Total: 860.70",
        "Average: 143.45",
        "Largest: 600.00 (Lodging, 2026-03-09)",
        "",
        "By category",
        "Lodging           600.00",
        "Travel            165.50",
        "Meals              95.20",
        "",
        "By month",
        "2026-03           842.70",
        "2026-04            18.00",
        "",
        "Rejected: 5",
        "  line 4: expected 4 columns but found 2",
        "  line 6: invalid amount 'abc'",
        "  line 9: invalid date '2026-13-01'",
        "  line 10: unknown category 'Parking'",
        "  line 11: amount must be positive",
        "```",
        "",
        "The list of individual expenses is gone. The rejected rows stay: someone has to fix those."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Three ways to format the same `decimal`. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "decimal total = 1234.5m;",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{total:F2}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{total:N2}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{total:C}\");"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "1234.50",
        "1,234.50",
        "$1,234.50"
      ],
      "explain": "`F2` is fixed-point: two decimals and nothing else. `N2` is *number*: two decimals plus thousands separators, which is what people expect for money. `C` adds the currency symbol of the current culture, here `$`. The report uses `N2`, because an expense file does not say which currency it is in."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Aggregates, and the empty list",
      "body": [
        "You have met the LINQ methods that boil a list down to one value:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "int count       = expenses.Count;",
        "decimal total   = expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount);",
        "decimal average = expenses.Average(e => e.Amount);",
        "Expense largest = expenses.OrderByDescending(e => e.Amount).First();",
        "```",
        "",
        "They do not all agree about an **empty** list. `Count` and `Sum` say `0`. `Average`, `Max`, `Min` and `First` have no sensible answer, so they throw `InvalidOperationException`.",
        "",
        "An input where every row was rejected is perfectly possible, so the program must decide what an empty report looks like **before** it calls any of them:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "if (expenses.Count == 0)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"No valid expenses.\");",
        "}",
        "else",
        "{",
        "    PrintSummary(expenses);",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "From here on each section of the report gets its own small method that takes the list it needs. The top of the file then reads like a table of contents.",
        "",
        "> **Tip:** A parameter may have the same name as a variable at the top of the file. Inside the method, the name means the parameter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`expenses` is an empty `List<Expense>`. Which of these lines throw an exception? Select all that apply.",
      "options": [
        "`expenses.Average(e => e.Amount)`",
        "`expenses.Max(e => e.Amount)`",
        "`expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount)`",
        "`expenses.Count`"
      ],
      "answer": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "explain": "There is no average or largest value of nothing, so those two throw. The sum of nothing is 0, and so is the count."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "The summary",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Replace the listing of every expense with a summary.",
        "",
        "Write `void PrintSummary(List<Expense> expenses)` that prints four lines: how many expenses, their total, their average, and the largest one with its category and date. All amounts use the `N2` format.",
        "",
        "Move the rejected rows into `void PrintRejected(List<Rejected> rejected)`. It prints an **empty line** first, then `Rejected: N` and the indented rows as before.",
        "",
        "If there are no valid expenses, print `No valid expenses.` instead of the summary. The rejected section is printed either way.",
        "",
        "`Describe` is no longer used: delete it. For the input from the briefing, print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Expenses: 6",
        "Total: 860.70",
        "Average: 143.45",
        "Largest: 600.00 (Lodging, 2026-03-09)",
        "",
        "Rejected: 5",
        "  line 4: expected 4 columns but found 2",
        "  line 6: invalid amount 'abc'",
        "  line 9: invalid date '2026-13-01'",
        "  line 10: unknown category 'Parking'",
        "  line 11: amount must be positive",
        "```",
        "",
        "If two expenses tie for largest, show the one that comes first in the input."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var expenses = new List<Expense>();",
        "var rejected = new List<Rejected>();",
        "",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "    if (line.StartsWith(\"date,\")) continue;",
        "",
        "    var result = ParseLine(lineNumber, line);",
        "    if (result is Parsed parsed)",
        "        expenses.Add(parsed.Expense);",
        "    else if (result is Rejected rejection)",
        "        rejected.Add(rejection);",
        "}",
        "",
        "foreach (var expense in expenses)",
        "    Console.WriteLine(Describe(expense));",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Valid: {expenses.Count}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Total: {expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount):F2}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Rejected: {rejected.Count}\");",
        "foreach (var rejection in rejected)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  line {rejection.LineNumber}: {rejection.Reason}\");",
        "",
        "ParseResult ParseLine(int lineNumber, string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', 4, StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"expected 4 columns but found {parts.Length}\");",
        "",
        "    if (!DateOnly.TryParseExact(parts[0], \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var date))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid date '{parts[0]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Category>(parts[1], ignoreCase: true, out var category) || !Enum.IsDefined(category))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"unknown category '{parts[1]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!decimal.TryParse(parts[2], CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var amount))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid amount '{parts[2]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (amount <= 0)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, \"amount must be positive\");",
        "",
        "    return new Parsed(new Expense(date, category, amount, parts[3]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Describe(Expense expense) =>",
        "    $\"{expense.Date:yyyy-MM-dd} | {expense.Category} | {expense.Amount:F2} | {expense.Description}\";",
        "",
        "enum Category { Travel, Meals, Lodging, Supplies, Other }",
        "",
        "record Expense(DateOnly Date, Category Category, decimal Amount, string Description);",
        "",
        "abstract record ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Parsed(Expense Expense) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Rejected(int LineNumber, string Reason) : ParseResult;"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var expenses = new List<Expense>();",
        "var rejected = new List<Rejected>();",
        "",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "    if (line.StartsWith(\"date,\")) continue;",
        "",
        "    var result = ParseLine(lineNumber, line);",
        "    if (result is Parsed parsed)",
        "        expenses.Add(parsed.Expense);",
        "    else if (result is Rejected rejection)",
        "        rejected.Add(rejection);",
        "}",
        "",
        "if (expenses.Count == 0)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"No valid expenses.\");",
        "}",
        "else",
        "{",
        "    PrintSummary(expenses);",
        "}",
        "",
        "PrintRejected(rejected);",
        "",
        "ParseResult ParseLine(int lineNumber, string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', 4, StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"expected 4 columns but found {parts.Length}\");",
        "",
        "    if (!DateOnly.TryParseExact(parts[0], \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var date))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid date '{parts[0]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Category>(parts[1], ignoreCase: true, out var category) || !Enum.IsDefined(category))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"unknown category '{parts[1]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (!decimal.TryParse(parts[2], CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var amount))",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, $\"invalid amount '{parts[2]}'\");",
        "",
        "    if (amount <= 0)",
        "        return new Rejected(lineNumber, \"amount must be positive\");",
        "",
        "    return new Parsed(new Expense(date, category, amount, parts[3]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintSummary(List<Expense> expenses)",
        "{",
        "    var largest = expenses.OrderByDescending(e => e.Amount).First();",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Expenses: {expenses.Count}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Total: {expenses.Sum(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Average: {expenses.Average(e => e.Amount):N2}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Largest: {largest.Amount:N2} ({largest.Category}, {largest.Date:yyyy-MM-dd})\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void PrintRejected(List<Rejected> rejected)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"Rejected: {rejected.Count}\");",
        "    foreach (var rejection in rejected)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  line {rejection.LineNumber}: {rejection.Reason}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "enum Category { Travel, Meals, Lodging, Supplies, Other }",
        "",
        "record Expense(DateOnly Date, Category Category, decimal Amount, string Description);",
        "",
        "abstract record ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Parsed(Expense Expense) : ParseResult;",
        "",
        "record Rejected(int LineNumber, string Reason) : ParseResult;"
      ],
