    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Grouping, and columns that line up",
      "body": [
        "*How much per category?* is a grouping question. `GroupBy` puts the expenses into one group per category. Each group has a `Key` and can be summed like any list.",
        "",
        "Give the result a name with a tiny record, then sort by it:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "var rows = expenses",
        "    .GroupBy(e => e.Category)",
        "    .Select(g => new SummaryRow(g.Key.ToString(), g.Sum(e => e.Amount)))",
        "    .OrderByDescending(row => row.Total);",
        "",
        "record SummaryRow(string Name, decimal Total);",
        "```",
        "",
        "To print a table, give every value a **width**. Inside `{ }`, a comma and a number come before the format:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{row.Name,-12}{row.Total,12:N2}\");",
        "```",
        "",
        "- `,-12` pads the name to 12 characters, text on the **left** (negative means left-aligned).",
        "- `,12:N2` formats the total as `N2`, then pads it to 12 characters with the number on the **right**, so the decimal points line up.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Lodging           600.00",
        "Travel            165.50",
        "```"
      ]
    },
